  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROTECTING HUMAN RIGHTS OF WOMEN,GIRLS &amp; VULNERABLE PEOPLE IN RURAL</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Protecting Human Rights Through Active Citizenry - Particularly The Rights Of Women And Girls And Vulnerable People In Rural Communities programme in South Africa, implemented by the Social Change Assistance Trust, aims to partner with rural local development agencies (LDAs) to build strong institutions that are able to respond to the cross-cutting issues of access to justice, gender, climate change, and youth. The objective of the grant are to build local agency by strengthening LDAs efforts to promote gender equality and address gender based violence. The key activities include, issuing grants to rural LDAs that focus on human rights, gender, GBV, climate change and youth and capacity building for women in LDAs.</narrative>
  </description>
